<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (The Earl Collins Foundation Scholarship is a competitive scholarship offered by the Missouri-Arkansas District of Kiwanis International for students entering accredited institutions such as universities, community colleges, trade schools, or academies. As college applications are around, this can be a great opportunity for seniors who are applying! Applicants are evaluated based on academic achievement, financial need, volunteerism, honors, education plans, and letters of recommendation, with bonus points for Key Club involvement or Kiwanis service. To apply, students must submit a complete application with all required documents to their local Kiwanis Club by January. The grants are for the individual chapters to be able to get some money for a project or on need basis. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
